  "title": "Alpine Forest",
  "category": "Places",
  "type": "Prima wilderness",
  "dek": "Cold woodland east of the Old Earth Hills. Shared exploration, a talking owl, a remembered mine and a fatal wolf encounter give the forest a history beyond its resources.",
  "facts": {
    "Region": "Prima",
    "Position": "East of Old Earth Hills",
    "Known resource": "Abandoned copper mine",
    "Dangers": "Alpine wolves · other wildlife",
    "Recorded exploration": "Pappy and Iridos; Severina and Cerwin; Ruben’s return to the copper mine",
    "Quarry relationship": "The approach heads toward the Alpine Forest, then turns off in the foothills"
  },
  "body": "<p>The Alpine Forest lies east of the <a href=\"#old-earth-hills\">Old Earth Hills</a> in Prima. Cold woodland, crags and trees high enough to conceal large animals make it a place to explore carefully. Its recorded visitors find useful materials and unexpected company; the same landscape also contains the wolves that kill Severina.</p><h2 id=\"prima-rp-forest-first\">Pappy and Iridos explore together</h2><p>Pappy arrives with a bearskin cloak and offers Iridos coffee. The cold reminds him of his mother’s stories, while Iridos is skeptical that they will find much beyond rock, ice and snow. They agree to make notes, and to run from danger they cannot handle.</p><p>Five enormous wolves bound down from a rocky crag. Iridos fights with a radiant halberd, and Pappy answers with lance and shield. When the last opponent is weakened, Pappy insists they finish it together. Afterward he offers food and begins harvesting, while Iridos admits that finding resources is not yet his skill.</p><p>Both think they could withstand another encounter, though that confidence is about their own condition at that moment. Their agreement to continue does not make the forest safe for everyone who follows.</p><h2 id=\"alpine-owl-and-memory\">The owl who knew stories of his parents</h2><p>Farther on, Pappy notices an enormous owl asleep in a tree hollow. Its coloring calls up a memory of an owl his mother used to speak with. He puts away his weapon, asks Iridos to hold, and addresses the creature respectfully. An offering of jerky gets its attention.</p><p>The owl calls itself Glides on Wings Unheard. It knows stories of Pappy’s parents, but explicitly says it did not know them and does not know their fate. The resemblance that moves Pappy is therefore not proof that this is the same owl from his childhood, or that the Alpine Forest is the frozen forest he remembers.</p><p>Pappy translates the conversation for Iridos. The owl asks no service of them and encourages him to be open to leaving Prima’s familiar shores again. When he asks where to repair his memories, it suggests looking within, then flies away. Pappy is left emotional rather than cured. He asks Iridos to let others know the owl has his protection; this is a personal promise, not ownership of the woodland.</p><p>Before turning back, they find a promontory overlooking the river that runs toward Pristinia. They begin following its banks. The scene gives them a way to orient their return without establishing a surveyed path through every part of the forest.</p><h2 id=\"prima-rp-forest-severina\">October 2025 · Severina and Cerwin</h2><p>Severina and Cerwin’s later expedition begins with a view from the trees. Cerwin admires the dense woodland and warns in general terms that beauty can hide danger. As Severina moves on, five alpine wolves surround her. Several approach without being seen.</p><p>Severina calls for Cerwin to shoot them and tries to keep fighting with her rapier. He wants to save her first, throws out meat and attempts to draw attention. The pack continues attacking. She falls unconscious; a wolf bites her again before being killed. The narrator records her last breath.</p><p>Cerwin kills the remaining wolf with a bolt driven into its eye. He declines to skin the animals or take trophies and chooses to carry her body toward Pristinia, hoping the Ale-Chemy Knights can help. That hope is not a recorded resurrection. Severina is active in later <a href=\"#before-survey\">survey</a> and <a href=\"#pristinia\">defense</a> records, but this forest scene does not explain her return.</p><h2 id=\"prima-rp-forest-copper\">The copper mine becomes a remembered place</h2><p>Ruben finds an abandoned copper mine in November 2025. When he locates it again in February 2026, he recognizes it as the mine he had told his companion about. The second visit is a return to a known site, rather than a new mine created by every successful search.</p><p>The recognition establishes a resource people can seek again. It does not establish a worked mine, a surveyed boundary, legal ownership or a constant measured yield. The record also preserves Ruben’s uncertainty: he had found nothing on several recent attempts before this success.</p><h2 id=\"prima-rp-forest-scale\">A landscape larger than its visitors</h2><p>The early regional description includes elk, old trees, a bear cave, an owl and the giant Ulmorodon grazing near the pine tops. It describes possibilities in this landscape; the narrated Pappy–Iridos visit specifically encounters wolves and the owl. It does not follow that every traveler sees every listed creature or that the giant has been tamed or successfully hunted.</p><h2 id=\"alpine-quarry-approach\">The quarry journey turns off in the foothills</h2><p>The formal quarry expedition supplies a useful limit on the forest’s geography. It travels through the <a href=\"#first-forest\">First Forest</a> in the Alpine Forest’s general direction, then veers off in the foothills. A bridge, frozen stream and wolf encounter precede another stretch of travel to the quarry.</p><p>The Alpine Forest is a direction and neighboring landscape in that account. The quarry is not thereby placed inside it, and its wolves are not automatically the same pack that attacked Severina or Pappy.</p><p class=\"place-context-links\"><strong>Connected histories</strong> <a href=\"#lady-severina\">Lady Severina Blackveil</a></p>",
